    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "Instead of receiving gold medals or trophies, winners of the Ancient Olympic
    Games were crowned with a wreath woven from olive branches. Wreaths were not
    only worn by athletes, but also appeared in religious festivals, celebrations,
    and works of art as a symbol of great honour, wisdom, peace, achievement, and
    respect. Olive trees were highly valued in Greece as they provided food, oil,
    wood, and shade. \n"
